#op: develop-value
A tool that composes lineages into one value binds the tip of one, compiled
on the development path, as that value holds it, with
`authoring.BindDevelopmentValue`. The development path tolerates the lenses
missing from the tip's edge only for the lineage that was compiled with them
missing. Here the value bound is the history alone, without the tip: it has
none of the tip's version, so it is not the lineage that was compiled.
-- ship/history/0.0.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
	b: int
}
-- ship/tip.thema --
Schema: {
	a: string
}
-- value.cue --
name: "ship"
schemas: {
	"0": {
		"0": {
			schema: {
				a: string
				b: int
			}
		}
	}
}
-- out/json --
{
  "diagnostics": [
    {
      "code": "E0626",
      "severity": "error",
      "headline": "the lineage to bind on the development path has versions v0.0, where ship was compiled with v0.0, v1.0",
      "notes": [
        {
          "label": "the development path tolerates the lenses missing from the tip's edge because ship was compiled with them missing, so it binds only the lineage ship was compiled to"
        }
      ],
      "help": [
        "bind the lineage that Compiled.File builds, as the larger value holds it"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "errors": 1,
    "warnings": 0,
    "notes": 0
  }
}
-- out/text --
